## (3) which change put a light element behind those bands

  The launcher did not change. Across the whole regression window the
  `.minivic-launcher`, `.minivic-launcher__pill` and `.minivic-launcher__disc`
  rules are byte-identical:

  $ git diff b02a8863 b9f5195e -- app/globals.css
    only two hunks:
      + .minivic-dock:hover { opacity: 1 !important }          (t_w1_mv2 6d007ad)
      + .minivic-dock .minivic-launcher { pointer-events: auto } (t_w1_mv2 6d007ad)
      - .minivic-panel height 100svh - 27.5rem
      + .minivic-panel height 100svh - 28rem                    (t_w1_red2 9deea50)
    Neither hunk touches the closed launcher's painted box.

  $ git diff --stat b02a8863 b9f5195e -- components/sections/About
    (empty — the About section is unchanged in the window)

  $ git log --oneline b02a8863..b9f5195e -- components/sections/Hero/
    9835a95 feat(hero): the light finds the figure … (G-H1 S2)
    9287089 feat(hero): the plane owns the frame: [data-plane=hero] wraps Scene
            + figure, portrait moves into the plane at §3 geometry,
            *role/location/caption move below the fold* … (G-H1 S1)

  INTRODUCING COMMIT: 9287089 (G-H1 S1). It is the only change in the window
  that alters the hero's height at 390, and every section below it slides by
  that amount. TC-MV-OCCLUDE-02 samples at a fixed scrollY (2 x 844 = 1688), so
  moving the page under the launcher is what put the About instrument stage's
  SVG behind the launcher's unpainted bands. Measured consequence, above:
  172/1659 pixels of the launcher's box above the ceiling, brightest
  rgb(171,171,171)/rgb(182,182,182) (the value moves between runs because the
  instrument stage animates) against a ceiling of 0.0968.

  CANDIDATES RULED OUT, with the diff that rules them out:
    6d007ad (mv2 :hover / pointer-events)  — adds no paint to the closed control
    9deea50 (red2 panel cap)               — .minivic-panel only; the panel is
                                             not mounted while the launcher is
                                             closed
    9835a95 (S2 poolPlate/uFigure)         — hero shader only, no layout
    1e1cb392 (S3)                          — no Hero/About/launcher file in the
                                             diff of the window

  NOT RUN: a per-commit rebuild bisect (5 exports x ~4 min + a browser each)
  does not fit the 30-minute cap with three other lanes on 4 cores. The commit
  above is named from the source diff plus the measurement in (2), which
  identifies the painting element rather than inferring it.

## (4) DECISION (docs/prompt.md §0.1)
  The defect is not a colour and it is not the page behind: a floating control
  cannot depend on what happens to be under it. The fix is that the launcher
  owns every pixel of its own footprint below 87.5rem — the widths where it
  floats over the measure. See 02-fix.md.
